# Pairs with ReadPositionHonest. The intent is inferred from the pin store: a
# rowless leaf is re-created when its pin is still the seeded Zero block pin or
# has no entry. The GC retires a rowless leaf's pin (PinRetire, #3101), after
# which the leaf reads as never created, so it is re-created empty over a WAL
# trimmed under its lost snapshot. This is why pin-store evidence cannot stand in
# for an explicit create path. The base takes no intent from the pin store.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestIntentFromRetiredPin
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a rowless leaf whose pin the GC retired is taken as never created
PERTURBS: Activate

--- FIND
    /\ row[l] \/ CreateIntent(l)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no pin entry, or only the seeded block pin, is taken as intent.
    /\ row[l] \/ Blocking(l) \/ pinHlc[l] = "gone"
--- END
--- FIND
SnapshotLoss == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the environment may destroy a snapshot or a leaf row.
SnapshotLoss == TRUE
--- END

--- FIND
MaxFaults == 1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the row and the snapshot both vanish: two faults.
MaxFaults == 2
--- END